Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 23:03:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(admin): seat fixtures for 1690 (a fact dated back) and
 1691 (an answer record)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Tester 49567 (rule B): two plate rows wait on state no chat can make on a
fresh seat. Both fixtures refuse any account that is not a fictional test
seat before reading anything else.

- POST /admin/test-accounts/:id/fixtures/stale-fact
  { phone, field_type (occupation|employer|city|industry), value, days_ago }
  writes the seat's own fact about one of its OWN contacts, dated back
  1–3650 days, with every confirm stamp cleared, so 1690's confirm can be
  checked at the moment of use.
- POST /admin/test-accounts/:id/fixtures/answer-record
  { goal_text, asked, yes, no, referred, first_answer_minutes_median }
  sets the seat's answer record under the field the goal text files under
  (askField), so 1691's wave order can be checked. The hourly recount
  rebuilds it once the seat is really asked.

